{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block importmap %}{{ importmap('games') }}{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
{{ include('games/_header.html.twig') }}

<main class="games">
    <h1>Claim a face in a group photo</h1>
    <p>Take a free place in a photo, then tell your AI assistant how you want to look. Everyone in the photo approves the final picture.</p>

    <h2>Join a game</h2>
    {% if joinable %}
        <ul class="cards">
            {% for game in joinable %}{{ include('games/_card.html.twig') }}{% endfor %}
        </ul>
    {% else %}
        <p class="quiet">No game has a free place right now. A new photo opens when a game ends.</p>
    {% endif %}
    <p><a href="{{ host_url }}">Host a game with your own photo</a>, with the host code.</p>
    <p class="quiet">An AI agent can play too: <a href="{{ path('app_agent_guide') }}">{{ url('app_agent_guide') }}</a> lists the open games and the steps.</p>

    <section class="how">
        <h2>How a game works</h2>
        <ol>
            <li>Pick a photo and type a name. Drupal gives you a seat in that game and signs your browser in.</li>
            <li>Click your face. A detector boxed each person when the photo arrived.</li>
            <li>Connect your AI assistant to the game's MCP server. It signs in as you, from the same browser.</li>
            <li>Ask it for a wish: "hide my face", "put me in the middle", "disguise me", "turn me to gold", "make me a cartoon", "repaint me as pixel art". A wish changes only your own place, and every player's page shows the new picture.</li>
            <li>When the picture suits you, approve it with a click. Once every player has approved, the game closes for good and a new photo opens.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>Under the hood</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>This page is a Symfony 8 app that keeps no game data. It reads the games from Drupal through the PHP MCP SDK, with a read-only token of its own from the OAuth client-credentials grant.</li>
            <li>Drupal 11, run by Drupack, holds the rules. Each game is a node with a state machine: open, then closed, or abandoned after a day without change.</li>
            <li>Your assistant talks to Drupal's MCP server directly, with tools such as <code>photo_get</code>, <code>claim_place</code>, <code>make_wish</code> and <code>paint_me</code>. It signs in with OAuth as your player account, so it can only change your place.</li>
            <li>A DETR model runs in PHP through Symfony AI's TransformersPhp bridge and finds the people in a new photo.</li>
            <li>A small local model reads each wish through Symfony AI, which turns its answer into a validated PHP object. Plain PHP code then crops, covers or repaints the photo.</li>
            <li>Only your own click approves a picture. Your assistant gets the approval page as a link, through MCP URL elicitation where the client supports it.</li>
            <li>A Mercure hub tells every open page when the picture changes.</li>
            <li>The prepared photos are public domain, from Wikimedia Commons. Each one is checked against its SHA-1 when it opens.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    {% if playing %}
        <h2>Being played</h2>
        <ul class="cards">
            {% for game in playing %}{{ include('games/_card.html.twig') }}{% endfor %}
        </ul>
    {% endif %}

    {% if over %}
        <h2>Finished</h2>
        <ul class="cards">
            {% for game in over %}{{ include('games/_card.html.twig') }}{% endfor %}
        </ul>
    {% endif %}
</main>
{% endblock %}
